    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5162" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμερ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without parts, indivisible,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				205e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prm.</u>
				138a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				231b3
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Virg.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; introduced into Latin by <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				40
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
				</span></i>
			 Aphr. <i><span class="en">
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				714.25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἀδιαστάτως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					33
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀ.</span> in Logic, <i>summa genera,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				100b2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>impartial,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρίσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Cal.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
